"thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 4058, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 4058, "cached_input": 29691, "input": 33751, "output": 175}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 35784, "other": 423, "system": 40398, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 4865}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 95867}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "f0ffaabc-b6f8-535c-80b1-6e20b5d2ebd8", "at": 1795658839.0401387, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 136501, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": "paper-repo", "execution_id": "f8ba3b57e4eb9ce2b461f9752ad18653", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "ea920450-ac7c-5516-a1f2-1b2647dfa919", "at": 1795658839.758, "until": 1795658839.7802155, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 136517, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "f8ba3b57e4eb9ce2b461f9752ad18653", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (6 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "9104ba05-9857-50cc-84d9-c28936018b1a", "at": 1795658839.783307, "until": 1795658840.6649795, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 136524, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": "paper-repo", "execution_id": "f8ba3b57e4eb9ce2b461f9752ad18653", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_012geedcAHeUhG4vyWd7WmTi", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /tmp && rm -rf ow && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" ow && cd ow && git log --oneline | head -3; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --stat; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD | head -80", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /tmp && rm -rf ow && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" ow && cd ow && git log --oneline | head -3; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --stat; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD | head -80"]], "output": "```console\n88410df Outline rev 20: record what the paper already says\n69adc08 Outline rev 20: Holme-Kim check, tail-and-clustering reading dropped (Brief rev 17)\n1946051 Outline rev 19: P7 'consistent with', Holme-Kim check weak support (Brief rev 16)\n Outline.md | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\ndiff --git a/Outline.md b/Outline.md\nindex 469f20a..9e518af 100644\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n@@ -101,4 +101,4 @@ Main text 9 pages including all figures and tables (references, appendix and che\n - **Rev. 18 record (Brief rev. 15).** (b): bias = s[HM(d_i)/AM(d_i)−1] (r 0.9988, RMS 0.0073, 60 runs), so \"falls with d\" is stated only with its condition: near-Poisson degrees (SBM, ER: −0.115, −0.025, +0.005); not for BA (−0.16 to −0.12), Stanford3 (−0.26 to −0.44, growing), ego-Facebook (−0.27 to −0.38), near-regular WS ≈ 0; the formula is exact for tree-like neighbourhoods and untested beyond these runs. (d) on real graphs: cause not diagnosed (C7). No verdict moves; `report` is asked for the two wordings.\n - **Rev. 19 record (Brief rev. 16).** Wording only: P7 is \"consistent with\" the non-identification account, not confirmation (the account was formulated after P5(ii) failed); a Holme–Kim check of the real-graph (d) reading is weak support and labelled so. Passed to `report` with the P7 table when it arrives.\n - **Rev. 8 record.** `idea` confirmed the thesis (`idea-repo`#7): headline pair is the regime map plus the bias non-identification; P2 worded as above; P1 states 0.55 without a cause; the real-graph threshold is a scope statement (check on existing data, `experiment-repo`#7); P6 added as C9.\n-- **Rev. 20 record (Brief rev. 17).** Holme–Kim check: HK behaves like BA, so the two-factor (tail + clustering) reading gains no support and is dropped as an explanation; the cause of the real-graph (d) behaviour stays open, with exposure spread named only as a description (Spearman −0.95 at d=20, +0.21 at d=80, 9 graphs, not a test). The (b) form s(HM/AM−1) predicts the realised bias on HK and LN without refitting (HK −0.141/−0.163/−0.129 vs −0.147/−0.164/−0.127; LN −0.311/−0.278/−0.305 vs −0.314/−0.274/−0.311 at d=20/5/80); \"falls with d\" does not hold for HK or LN, as the near-Poisson condition says. The paper's Discussion and §5.2 call the tail-and-clustering reading a hypothesis: `report` is asked to drop it, once the HK table is delivered.\n+- **Rev. 20 record (Brief rev. 17).** Holme–Kim check: HK behaves like BA, so the two-factor (tail + clustering) reading gains no support and is dropped as an explanation; the cause of the real-graph (d) behaviour stays open, with exposure spread named only as a description (Spearman −0.95 at d=20, +0.21 at d=80, 9 graphs, not a test). The (b) form s(HM/AM−1) predicts the realised bias on HK and LN without refitting (HK −0.141/−0.163/−0.129 vs −0.147/−0.164/−0.127; LN −0.311/−0.278/−0.305 vs −0.314/−0.274/−0.311 at d=20/5/80); \"falls with d\" does not hold for HK or LN, as the near-Poisson condition says. Checked against `paper-repo` `dev` 8e015dd: §5.2 already claims no two-factor reading (tail alone and clustering alone do not reproduce it; the spread is a description), the Discussion only says thinning also changes clustering and the tail, and the appendix P7 paragraph says the block does not test the account and S_adj is not cited as evidence. One sentence is owed when the HK table is delivered: HK behaves like BA, so the tail-plus-clustering reading is not supported.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian